## Hints for Future Agents
- The [1m] alias row is purely defensive: logs only ever show bare
  "claude-fable-5" so far, but opus[1m] (26 entries) proved [1m]-suffixed
  strings do occur in these logs and previously fell to default silently.
  Rates are identical because Fable 5 has no long-context premium.
- If Anthropic later ships a Fable fast tier, add "claude-fable-5:fast" (and
  "claude-fable-5[1m]:fast") — the parse path needs no changes.
- Pricing applies at display time; cached entries reprice automatically, no
  --clear-cache needed. CacheVersion still 5.
- Log-scan gotcha (re-confirmed): filenames under ~/.claude/projects start with
  "-", so use `grep -rh PATTERN dir` or pass `--` before filenames.

